<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.9.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00203</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.9.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5e85d820-6e2f-413f-b323-68f98bf21359</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will practice solving for a specific variable to obtain an expression defined in terms of the other variables. Through the lesson’s activities you will see that this process allows you to solve problems more efficiently.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item>Solve an equation for one of the variables.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
      <list id="list-00002">
        <item>1.9.1: Rearranging an Equation in Three Variables</item>
        <item>1.9.2: Writing an Equation to Represent a Constraint<list id="list-00003">
            <item>1.9.2: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.9.2: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.9.3: Writing and Rearranging Equations in Two Variables<list id="list-00004">
            <item>1.9.3: Self Check</item>
            <item>1.9.3: Additional Resources</item>
          </list>
        </item>
        <item>1.9.4: Solving for a Specified Variable</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00004">After that, you'll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
      <list id="list-00005">
        <item>1.9.5: Practice</item>
        <item>1.9.6: Lesson Summary</item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>